    "# Quiz: Introduction to natural language processing\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-6-1-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What does NLP stand for in these lessons?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Neural Language Processing</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The N in NLP stands for natural, not neural. NLP is about how computers process natural, or human, languages.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>natural language processing</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. NLP is natural language processing: how computers process 'natural', or human, languages.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Natural Linguistic Processing</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The L stands for language. NLP is natural language processing, about how computers process human languages.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-6-1-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Eliza was an early bot that acted as a computer</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>therapist</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Eliza was a computer 'therapist' that asked people questions and seemed to understand their answers.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>doctor</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The lesson calls Eliza a computer 'therapist'. It asked people questions and seemed to understand their answers.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>nurse</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Eliza acted as a computer therapist. It asked people questions and seemed to understand their answers.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-6-1-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Alan Turing's 'Turing Test' tried to determine if a computer was</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>indistinguishable from a human</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. That is part of it, but Turing also asked if such a computer could be said to be thinking.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>thinking</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. That is part of it, but the test also checks if a person can tell the computer apart from a human.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>both of the above</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. If a person could not tell the computer from a human, Turing asked if the computer could be said to be thinking.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
